# Nothing generated, compiled or binary belongs in this tree.
#
# The extraction from testsAndMisc carried the bytecode caches across as
# tracked files, so every `python -m pytest tests` left 30 modified .pyc
# blobs in `git status` and any wide `git add` swept them into a commit.
# They are untracked as of the commit that adds this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode and test artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary and media families. Same extension list the shared binary gate
# blocks, so "git ignored it" and "the hook would have rejected it" cannot
# disagree. A file a build genuinely cannot run without needs BOTH a `!`
# override here and an entry in .binary-allowlist -- this repo is shell and
# Python only and currently needs neither.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.ico
*.bmp
*.tiff
*.tif
*.psd
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.wav
*.avi
*.mkv
*.flac
*.ogg
*.wma
*.aac
*.m4a
*.mov
*.wmv
*.flv
*.zip
*.tar
*.gz
*.tgz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.7z
*.rar
*.pdf
*.doc
*.docx
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.ppt
*.pptx
*.ttf
*.woff
*.woff2
*.eot
*.otf
*.o
*.so
*.a
*.exe
*.dll
*.dylib
*.class
*.apkg
*.bin
*.flat
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
